# StressRouteClassifier.mlmodel — PLACEHOLDER

This file is a placeholder. The actual trained Core ML model is generated by
running the training script:

    swift MLTraining/TrainStressModel.swift

Prerequisites:
  - macOS 12+ (Create ML framework)
  - Xcode Command Line Tools installed

The script will:
  1. Load MLTraining/StressTrainingData.csv (500 synthetic rows)
  2. Train an MLBoostedTreeRegressor targeting "stress_score"
  3. Export the compiled .mlmodel to this location

Model inputs:
  - traffic_density     Double  (0.0 – 1.0)
  - junction_complexity Double  (0.0 – 1.0)
  - road_type           String  ("residential" | "arterial" | "highway" | "motorway")
  - time_of_day         Double  (0.0 – 23.99, representing hour)
  - weather_input       Double  (0.0 – 1.0, where 1.0 = severe weather)

Model output:
  - stress_score        Double  (0.0 – 100.0)

Until the real model is generated, StressScoreService will automatically fall
back to StressScoreFallback, which implements the same weighted formula used
to generate the training data.
